## Findings
1. blocking — brief:78 `planUse` chooses every at-or-before-start value as the baseline before rejecting an older reset. A plausible stale Codex reading—5/reset 200, then stale 95/reset 100 before the cycle, then 6/reset 200—makes done and rung cost report +0 instead of +1, and no existing test catches it. Replace the plan-order clause with: “Before choosing or replacing the baseline, `planUse` passes over a line whose reset instant is earlier than the latest already seen; `W-495-b1` pins the stale-before-start sequence above.” [severity: S1] [design: keeps] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: packages/cli/src/w495.test.ts W-495-b1 stale-before-start case
2. blocking — brief:48 A missed sample at reset can leave the old week at 2% and the first new-week sample at 3%; the specified rise-first rule makes done and rung cost add +1 rather than the new week’s whole +3, while the existing reset test covers only a fall. Replace the reset rule with: “After rejecting an earlier reset, a later reset instant adds the reading’s whole value and sets the level regardless of whether that value rose, stayed equal or fell; only a same or unknown reset uses the rise/fall rules.” [severity: S1] [design: changes] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: packages/cli/src/w495.test.ts W-495-b1 rising-reset and equal-reset cases
3. advisory — brief:58 The claimed one-point endpoint bound is false: using the last reading before `from` can include arbitrarily much pre-span use, while stopping at the last reading before `to` can omit arbitrarily much in-span use. Replace the endpoint limit with: “The observable span starts from the last sample at or before `from` and ends at the last sample at or before `to`; it may include use between the baseline sample and `from` and omit use between the final sample and `to`, with no one-point bound on either sampling gap.” [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: unrecorded endpoint use has no automated oracle, so this must remain a stated limit
4. advisory — brief:62 `git log master` traverses commits reachable through merged side branches, so a record greenlit on such a branch yields that branch commit’s committer time, not necessarily its PR-land time. Replace the greenlight limit with: “The greenlight is the committer time of the oldest commit reachable from master whose diff adds or removes the matching `state: greenlit` line; when that commit came from a merged branch, its branch timestamp—not the PR-land timestamp—is used.” [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: packages/cli/src/w495.test.ts W-495-b3 branch-greenlight case
5. advisory — brief:83 The Input domain omits the new kept script’s repository argument, ids, two HTML files, shipped-row/PR/spend-cell grammar and git subprocess boundary. Replace brief:83 with a row specifying `checkpoint-rows.mts(repo, ids)` as accepting readable progress and masthead files, one shipped row and decimal PR per id, a matching first-parent land, and a recognized spend prefix, rejected before either write by specified `rewriteCheckpointRows`, with the script’s `git` wrapper aborting on `execFileSync` failure; then retain the reused-gates row as row 7. [severity: S4] [class: spec×input-without-named-rejector] — check: none: Input-domain reader coverage has no automated semantic rule
6. advisory — brief:64 The rung-cost promise neither states how its three spec-log readers disagree nor accounts for `appendReading` failing, when the printed cost can exclude the rung’s current values. Replace the line with: “Each performed rung prints `spanCost` through its clock from persisted readable readings; the first signature is the earliest accepted log across master, the opus branch/worktree and the main checkout—refs omit untracked or uncommitted logs, filesystem sources include them, and unreadable entries are skipped—and if appending the rung reading fails, cost uses prior readable readings or says none.” [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-contract-not-declared] — check: packages/cli/src/w495.test.ts W-495-b4 divergent-source and append-failure cases

